  m_Name: 5_SurvivalOutsideHost
  m_EditorClassIdentifier: 
  Title: 'Survival Outside Host:'
  Description: Serotype Dublin can survive in faeces spread on concrete, rubber, and
    polyester for almost six years.  Flies have been shown to excrete certain serotypes
    for 8 days and bed bugs can excrete bacilli for up to 21 days. Certain serotypes
    have been shown to survive on fingertips for up to 80 minutes, depending on the
    inoculum size. Salmonella serotypes have been found to live up to 63 days on lettuce,
    231 days on parsley, 32 weeks in pecans, 10 months on refrigerated cheddar cheese,
    9 months in butter, up to 63 days in frozen yogurt, and up to 20 weeks on frozen
    minced beef and chicken.
